IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cf66-nouns`

-- Row il-66. THE FOUR ITEMS (I1 to I4), as typed values. Each defect has a sound value beside it, or the row says that none was found.
-- "KT" is Kovetz HaTakanot, the regulations series of the official gazette; the number after it is the issue number, not a year. The official pages were read from page images of whole issues taken from olaw.org.il, a private archive of the printed issues; the issues are not deposited, only cropped images of the lines read.
-- ITEM I1: the Fees Regulations, as made, define "pre-trial session" by rules 143 and 214 (with a letter) of the 1984 Civil Procedure Regulations; the amending regulations in KT 8085 cancel regulations 132 to 258 of the 1984 Regulations, with a saving clause for earlier proceedings.
-- ITEM I2: the 2021 amendment of the Fees Regulations opens with a power cited as "83(3)" of the Courts Law; the consolidation of the Courts Law prints s 83 with subsections lettered (א) and (ב), and the fees in paragraph (3) of (א).
-- ITEM I3: the annual notice KT 7199 prints two different figures for the threshold that items 8 and 22 use.
-- ITEM I4: three dated instruments about item 36 of the Schedule, in the order of their dates.
-- Each reading says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in cf66-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource texts are not official, and anything resting only on them is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
-- The row states what each instrument prints. It does not say that the Regulations, the Law or anyone is wrong, and it does not say what a court would do or who gains. It names no person who signed.
-- ASCII quotation marks stand for the printed ones.

§ `I1: the definition of the pre-trial session cites rules 143 and 214 of the 1984 Regulations`

